"Experimental Features: After this many commands, make codecierge confirm that you intend to keep it enabled." = "Experimental Features: After this many commands, make codecierge confirm that you intend to keep it enabled.";
"Experimental Features: Aggressively keep windows on the screen they were configured to be on" = "Experimental Features: Aggressively keep windows on the screen they were configured to be on";
"Experimental Features: Allow function keys to be handled by macOS text input system.\nThis supports using function keys with modifiers as compose/dead keys in custom keyboard layouts." = "Experimental Features: Allow function keys to be handled by macOS text input system.\nThis supports using function keys with modifiers as compose/dead keys in custom keyboard layouts.";
"Experimental Features: Allow variable window sizes in tmux integration.\nRequres tmux version 2.9 or later." = "Experimental Features: Allow variable window sizes in tmux integration.\nRequres tmux version 2.9 or later.";
"Experimental Features: Auto-detect paragraph writing direction based on the first strong directional character?\nRequires right-to-left text support to be enabled." = "Experimental Features: Auto-detect paragraph writing direction based on the first strong directional character?\nRequires right-to-left text support to be enabled.";
"Experimental Features: Automatically restore keyboard mode when an ssh session ends?" = "Experimental Features: Automatically restore keyboard mode when an ssh session ends?";
"Experimental Features: Automatically search for selected text after making a selection?" = "Experimental Features: Automatically search for selected text after making a selection?";
"Experimental Features: Cache per-row GPU build output?\nSkips rebuilding the glyph and color data for rows whose content and configuration have not changed since the last frame. Experimental." = "Experimental Features: Cache per-row GPU build output?\nSkips rebuilding the glyph and color data for rows whose content and configuration have not changed since the last frame. Experimental.";
"Experimental Features: Clear bell icon when a session becomes active.\nWhen off, you must type in the session to clear the bell icon." = "Experimental Features: Clear bell icon when a session becomes active.\nWhen off, you must type in the session to clear the bell icon.";
"Experimental Features: Detect base unicode characters with lookup table.\nApple's algorithm for segmenting composed characters makes bad choices, such as for Tamil. Enable this to reduce text overlapping." = "Experimental Features: Detect base unicode characters with lookup table.\nApple's algorithm for segmenting composed characters makes bad choices, such as for Tamil. Enable this to reduce text overlapping.";
"Experimental Features: Disable metal renderer when idle to save CPU utilization?\nRequires Metal renderer" = "Experimental Features: Disable metal renderer when idle to save CPU utilization?\nRequires Metal renderer";
"Experimental Features: Disclaim ownership of children.\nBy enabling this, when launching a Cocoa app from a terminal window TCC should attribute ownership to the app, not iTerm2, for permissions. In order for changes to this setting to take effect, you must kill iTermServer." = "Experimental Features: Disclaim ownership of children.\nBy enabling this, when launching a Cocoa app from a terminal window TCC should attribute ownership to the app, not iTerm2, for permissions. In order for changes to this setting to take effect, you must kill iTermServer.";
"Experimental Features: Dismember scroll view for better GPU performance?\nThis enables a dangerous hack that might improve drawing performance on macOS 10.14 only." = "Experimental Features: Dismember scroll view for better GPU performance?\nThis enables a dangerous hack that might improve drawing performance on macOS 10.14 only.";
"Experimental Features: Enable AquaSKK bugfix?" = "Experimental Features: Enable AquaSKK bugfix?";
"Experimental Features: Enable Channels feature?" = "Experimental Features: Enable Channels feature?";
"Experimental Features: Enable browser-style profiles?\nYou must restart iTerm2 for this to take effect." = "Experimental Features: Enable browser-style profiles?\nYou must restart iTerm2 for this to take effect.";
"Experimental Features: Enable character accent menu.\nThis disables the ordinary key repeat behavior for press-and-hold. You must restart iTerm2 for this change to take effect." = "Experimental Features: Enable character accent menu.\nThis disables the ordinary key repeat behavior for press-and-hold. You must restart iTerm2 for this change to take effect.";
"Experimental Features: Enable low-latency updates of the current foreground job" = "Experimental Features: Enable low-latency updates of the current foreground job";
"Experimental Features: Enable more compact logging when using auto composer?\nThis will avoid logging raw data in your prompt and your interactions with it. Instead, the prompt is logged once in plain text and the command is logged when sent." = "Experimental Features: Enable more compact logging when using auto composer?\nThis will avoid logging raw data in your prompt and your interactions with it. Instead, the prompt is logged once in plain text and the command is logged when sent.";
"Experimental Features: Enable multi-server daemon.\nA new implementation of session restoration that combines daemon processes." = "Experimental Features: Enable multi-server daemon.\nA new implementation of session restoration that combines daemon processes.";
"Experimental Features: Enable restorable state controller?\nThis makes window restoration more reliable." = "Experimental Features: Enable restorable state controller?\nThis makes window restoration more reliable.";
"Experimental Features: Enable support for REP (Repeat previous character) escape sequence?" = "Experimental Features: Enable support for REP (Repeat previous character) escape sequence?";
"Experimental Features: Escape file names with single quotes instead of backslashes.\nThis is intended for users of xonsh, which does not accept backslash escaping." = "Experimental Features: Escape file names with single quotes instead of backslashes.\nThis is intended for users of xonsh, which does not accept backslash escaping.";
"Experimental Features: Extend background color into margins in alternate screen mode?" = "Experimental Features: Extend background color into margins in alternate screen mode?";
"Experimental Features: Fast regular expression evaluation for triggers.\nThis is experimental because it could potentially change how regular expressions are interpreted." = "Experimental Features: Fast regular expression evaluation for triggers.\nThis is experimental because it could potentially change how regular expressions are interpreted.";
"Experimental Features: Flag emoji render full-width" = "Experimental Features: Flag emoji render full-width";
"Experimental Features: Host and port for proxy for AI requests.\ni.e., example.com:8080" = "Experimental Features: Host and port for proxy for AI requests.\ni.e., example.com:8080";
"Experimental Features: Improved support for input method editors like AquaSKK." = "Experimental Features: Improved support for input method editors like AquaSKK.";
"Experimental Features: Kill sessions on logout.\nA possible fix for issue 4147." = "Experimental Features: Kill sessions on logout.\nA possible fix for issue 4147.";
"Experimental Features: List of fonts to use alternate rounding algorithm for line height calculation.\nThis fixes consolas and emulates Terminal.app’s behavior on macOS 10.15. This is a comma-delimited list of font family substrings." = "Experimental Features: List of fonts to use alternate rounding algorithm for line height calculation.\nThis fixes consolas and emulates Terminal.app’s behavior on macOS 10.15. This is a comma-delimited list of font family substrings.";
"Experimental Features: Log a histogram of non-ASCII string lengths periodically.\nUseful for tuning the async pre-conversion minimum string length." = "Experimental Features: Log a histogram of non-ASCII string lengths periodically.\nUseful for tuning the async pre-conversion minimum string length.";
"Experimental Features: Make the tab bar a titlebar accessory view in Big Sur?" = "Experimental Features: Make the tab bar a titlebar accessory view in Big Sur?";
"Experimental Features: Make uploads with it2ul really fast." = "Experimental Features: Make uploads with it2ul really fast.";
"Experimental Features: Maximum bytes of outstanding async pre-conversions.\nWhen this limit is reached, new strings are converted synchronously on the mutation thread." = "Experimental Features: Maximum bytes of outstanding async pre-conversions.\nWhen this limit is reached, new strings are converted synchronously on the mutation thread.";
"Experimental Features: Minimum string length (in UTF-16 code units) to dispatch for async pre-conversion." = "Experimental Features: Minimum string length (in UTF-16 code units) to dispatch for async pre-conversion.";
"Experimental Features: Mouse wheel always scrolls when scroll bars are visible" = "Experimental Features: Mouse wheel always scrolls when scroll bars are visible";
"Experimental Features: Post fake flags-changed events when remapping modifiers with an event tap.\nThis is an attempt to work around incompatibilities with AltTab in issue 10220." = "Experimental Features: Post fake flags-changed events when remapping modifiers with an event tap.\nThis is an attempt to work around incompatibilities with AltTab in issue 10220.";
"Experimental Features: Pre-convert long non-ASCII strings on a background queue.\nThis decouples preconversion from the parser thread for better throughput." = "Experimental Features: Pre-convert long non-ASCII strings on a background queue.\nThis decouples preconversion from the parser thread for better throughput.";
"Experimental Features: Pre-convert non-ASCII strings to screen characters on the parser thread.\nThis exploits parallelism between parsing and screen mutation for better performance." = "Experimental Features: Pre-convert non-ASCII strings to screen characters on the parser thread.\nThis exploits parallelism between parsing and screen mutation for better performance.";
"Experimental Features: Prompt to send to LLM for Codecierge when it is NOT able to execute commands automatically.\n$GOAL and $CONTEXT are replaced with the user-specified goal and info about the running environment, respectively." = "Experimental Features: Prompt to send to LLM for Codecierge when it is NOT able to execute commands automatically.\n$GOAL and $CONTEXT are replaced with the user-specified goal and info about the running environment, respectively.";
"Experimental Features: Prompt to send to LLM for Codecierge when it is able to execute commands automatically.\n$GOAL and $CONTEXT are replaced with the user-specified goal and info about the running environment, respectively." = "Experimental Features: Prompt to send to LLM for Codecierge when it is able to execute commands automatically.\n$GOAL and $CONTEXT are replaced with the user-specified goal and info about the running environment, respectively.";
"Experimental Features: Reduce number of frames in flight when GPU can't produce drawables quickly." = "Experimental Features: Reduce number of frames in flight when GPU can't produce drawables quickly.";
"Experimental Features: Report 16-bit color values to OSC 4 and 10 through 19.\nWorks around a bug in older vim where they could not properly parse 8-bit values." = "Experimental Features: Report 16-bit color values to OSC 4 and 10 through 19.\nWorks around a bug in older vim where they could not properly parse 8-bit values.";
"Experimental Features: Report multiple mouse scroll events when scrolling quickly?" = "Experimental Features: Report multiple mouse scroll events when scrolling quickly?";
"Experimental Features: Reset colors at shell prompt?\nUses shell integration to detect a shell prompt and, if enabled, resets colors to their defaults." = "Experimental Features: Reset colors at shell prompt?\nUses shell integration to detect a shell prompt and, if enabled, resets colors to their defaults.";
"Experimental Features: Right-justify lines in paragraphs with base writing direction of right-to-left?\nRequires BOTH “right-to-left text support” and “auto-detect paragraph writing detection” to be enabled." = "Experimental Features: Right-justify lines in paragraphs with base writing direction of right-to-left?\nRequires BOTH “right-to-left text support” and “auto-detect paragraph writing detection” to be enabled.";
"Experimental Features: SSH URLs respect the path.\nThey run the command: ssh -t \"cd $$PATH$$; exec \\$SHELL -l\"" = "Experimental Features: SSH URLs respect the path.\nThey run the command: ssh -t \"cd $$PATH$$; exec \\$SHELL -l\"";
"Experimental Features: Save unlimited amount of window contents.\nThis is going to be slow unless you enable SQLite-based window restoration too." = "Experimental Features: Save unlimited amount of window contents.\nThis is going to be slow unless you enable SQLite-based window restoration too.";
"Experimental Features: Set LC_TERMINAL=iTerm2.\nopenssh and mosh pass this to hosts you connect to. It communicates the current terminal emulator. This is useful for enabling terminal emulator-specific features." = "Experimental Features: Set LC_TERMINAL=iTerm2.\nopenssh and mosh pass this to hosts you connect to. It communicates the current terminal emulator. This is useful for enabling terminal emulator-specific features.";
"Experimental Features: Show inline images at Retina resolution." = "Experimental Features: Show inline images at Retina resolution.";
"Experimental Features: Show prompt locations in scroll bar?\nChanging this setting will not affect existing sessions until you restart. You must also enable “Show search result and prompt locations in scroll bar” for this to take effect." = "Experimental Features: Show prompt locations in scroll bar?\nChanging this setting will not affect existing sessions until you restart. You must also enable “Show search result and prompt locations in scroll bar” for this to take effect.";
"Experimental Features: Show search result and prompt locations in scroll bar.\nChanging this setting will not affect existing sessions until you restart." = "Experimental Features: Show search result and prompt locations in scroll bar.\nChanging this setting will not affect existing sessions until you restart.";
"Experimental Features: Stamp frame numbers into the iTerm2 Buddy live stream?\nDraws a monotonic counter onto each streamed video frame, for debugging the phone’s live session view." = "Experimental Features: Stamp frame numbers into the iTerm2 Buddy live stream?\nDraws a monotonic counter onto each streamed video frame, for debugging the phone’s live session view.";
"Experimental Features: Store window restoration state in SQLite" = "Experimental Features: Store window restoration state in SQLite";
"Experimental Features: Support DECSET 1036?\nThis allows apps in the terminal to control whether the option key sends esc+ or acts like a regular option key." = "Experimental Features: Support DECSET 1036?\nThis allows apps in the terminal to control whether the option key sends esc+ or acts like a regular option key.";
"Experimental Features: Support modifier remapping for keystrokes originated by Synergy." = "Experimental Features: Support modifier remapping for keystrokes originated by Synergy.";
"Experimental Features: Support variation selector 16 making emoji fullwidth in all modes?" = "Experimental Features: Support variation selector 16 making emoji fullwidth in all modes?";
"Experimental Features: Support variation selector 16 making emoji fullwidth outside of alternate screen mode?" = "Experimental Features: Support variation selector 16 making emoji fullwidth outside of alternate screen mode?";
"Experimental Features: Trackpad scrolls fast?\nSet to No for legacy scrolling speed." = "Experimental Features: Trackpad scrolls fast?\nSet to No for legacy scrolling speed.";
"Experimental Features: Treat the equals sign on the numeric keypad as a key on the numeric keypad.\nFor mysterious reasons, macOS does not treat this key as belonging to the numeric keypad. Enable this setting to work around the bug." = "Experimental Features: Treat the equals sign on the numeric keypad as a key on the numeric keypad.\nFor mysterious reasons, macOS does not treat this key as belonging to the numeric keypad. Enable this setting to work around the bug.";
"Experimental Features: Use a more theoretically correct technique to measure line height.\nYou must restart iTerm2 or adjust a session's font size for this change to take effect." = "Experimental Features: Use a more theoretically correct technique to measure line height.\nYou must restart iTerm2 or adjust a session's font size for this change to take effect.";
"Experimental Features: Use modern scroll wheel accumulator.\nThis should support wheel mice better and feel more natural." = "Experimental Features: Use modern scroll wheel accumulator.\nThis should support wheel mice better and feel more natural.";
"Experimental Features: Use synchronized Metal drawable presentation?\nDefers drawable acquisition until rendering completes, presents synchronously with Core Animation, and acquires drawables on the private render queue. May improve frame rates." = "Experimental Features: Use synchronized Metal drawable presentation?\nDefers drawable acquisition until rendering completes, presents synchronously with Core Animation, and acquires drawables on the private render queue. May improve frame rates.";
"Experimental Features: When right-to-left text support is enabled, also support it in alternate screen mode?" = "Experimental Features: When right-to-left text support is enabled, also support it in alternate screen mode?";
"Experimental Features: When splitting a pane, use the profile with local modifications, not the backing profile." = "Experimental Features: When splitting a pane, use the profile with local modifications, not the backing profile.";
"Experimental Features: iTerm2 Buddy live stream: maximum capture-time lead, in milliseconds.\nThe host stops sending new frames once it is more than this far ahead of the last frame the phone acknowledged, then resumes when the phone catches up. Larger values tolerate more link latency at the cost of a live view that can lag further behind. Only the frame rate is affected; per-frame quality is unchanged." = "Experimental Features: iTerm2 Buddy live stream: maximum capture-time lead, in milliseconds.\nThe host stops sending new frames once it is more than this far ahead of the last frame the phone acknowledged, then resumes when the phone catches up. Larger values tolerate more link latency at the cost of a live view that can lag further behind. Only the frame rate is affected; per-frame quality is unchanged.";
"Experimental Features: iTerm2 Buddy live stream: maximum phone decode-queue depth.\nThe host stops sending new frames once the phone reports more than this many frames queued for decode/display, then resumes as the queue drains. Larger values let more frames pile up on the phone before backing off. Only the frame rate is affected; per-frame quality is unchanged." = "Experimental Features: iTerm2 Buddy live stream: maximum phone decode-queue depth.\nThe host stops sending new frames once the phone reports more than this many frames queued for decode/display, then resumes as the queue drains. Larger values let more frames pile up on the phone before backing off. Only the frame rate is affected; per-frame quality is unchanged.";
"Experimental Features: iTerm2 Buddy live stream: video bitrate multiplier.\nScales the resolution-derived encoder bitrate. Values above 1 make streamed text sharper at the cost of bandwidth; values below 1 save bandwidth at the cost of sharpness. The result is still clamped to the stream’s minimum and ceiling bitrates." = "Experimental Features: iTerm2 Buddy live stream: video bitrate multiplier.\nScales the resolution-derived encoder bitrate. Values above 1 make streamed text sharper at the cost of bandwidth; values below 1 save bandwidth at the cost of sharpness. The result is still clamped to the stream’s minimum and ceiling bitrates.";
"Experimental Features: iTerm2 Buddy push notifications: minimum seconds between wakeup pushes.\nA wakeup push tells the paired phone to fetch every new message and alert at once, so several in quick succession are wasteful and can leave a later one with nothing to show (the generic “Your agent has an update.” placeholder). The host sends the first wakeup immediately, then coalesces any that follow within this interval into a single trailing wakeup. Lower values notify sooner but coalesce less; higher values coalesce bursts more aggressively." = "Experimental Features: iTerm2 Buddy push notifications: minimum seconds between wakeup pushes.\nA wakeup push tells the paired phone to fetch every new message and alert at once, so several in quick succession are wasteful and can leave a later one with nothing to show (the generic “Your agent has an update.” placeholder). The host sends the first wakeup immediately, then coalesces any that follow within this interval into a single trailing wakeup. Lower values notify sooner but coalesce less; higher values coalesce bursts more aggressively.";
