"General: $PATH used when running git for the status bar component.\nChange this to use a custom install of git. You must restart iTerm2 for a change here to take effect." = "General: $PATH used when running git for the status bar component.\nChange this to use a custom install of git. You must restart iTerm2 for a change here to take effect.";
"General: 1Password account name.\nThis is used if you’ve enabled the 1Password integration in the password manager. Use `op account list` to get the list of accounts. This can be an account shorthand, sign-in address, account ID, or user ID." = "General: 1Password account name.\nThis is used if you’ve enabled the 1Password integration in the password manager. Use `op account list` to get the list of accounts. This can be an account shorthand, sign-in address, account ID, or user ID.";
"General: Add a 'Dynamic' tag to dynamic profiles.\nWhen enabled, dynamic profiles will have a 'Dynamic' tag added to them, which can be used to filter or identify them." = "General: Add a 'Dynamic' tag to dynamic profiles.\nWhen enabled, dynamic profiles will have a 'Dynamic' tag added to them, which can be used to filter or identify them.";
"General: Add status bar icon when excluded from dock?\nWhen you turn on “Exclude from Dock and ⌘-Tab Application Switcher” a status bar icon is added to the menu bar so you can switch the setting back off. Disable this to remove the status bar icon. Doing so makes it very hard to get to Settings. You must restart iTerm2 after changing this setting." = "General: Add status bar icon when excluded from dock?\nWhen you turn on “Exclude from Dock and ⌘-Tab Application Switcher” a status bar icon is added to the menu bar so you can switch the setting back off. Disable this to remove the status bar icon. Doing so makes it very hard to get to Settings. You must restart iTerm2 after changing this setting.";
"General: Allow pairing a companion iOS device?\nOff by default while this feature is in development. When off, the Companion Device Settings menu item is hidden. Managed environments can also use this to disable the feature. The user defaults key is `CompanionPairingAllowed`." = "General: Allow pairing a companion iOS device?\nOff by default while this feature is in development. When off, the Companion Device Settings menu item is hidden. Managed environments can also use this to disable the feature. The user defaults key is `CompanionPairingAllowed`.";
"General: Allow the standard system menu on window Zoom buttons to open?\nmacOS has a bug that makes the app hang. Since this is a rarely used menu, it is disabled by default." = "General: Allow the standard system menu on window Zoom buttons to open?\nmacOS has a bug that makes the app hang. Since this is a rarely used menu, it is disabled by default.";
"General: Allow the use of large language model APIs?\nThe purpose of this setting is to make it easy for managed environments to disable the use of LLMs. The user defaults key is `GenerativeAIAllowed`." = "General: Allow the use of large language model APIs?\nThe purpose of this setting is to make it easy for managed environments to disable the use of LLMs. The user defaults key is `GenerativeAIAllowed`.";
"General: Bundle ID of browser to open URLs with.\nLeave empty to use system default." = "General: Bundle ID of browser to open URLs with.\nLeave empty to use system default.";
"General: Buttons in modal alerts indicate keyboard shortcuts.\nDo you miss Windows 95? I do." = "General: Buttons in modal alerts indicate keyboard shortcuts.\nDo you miss Windows 95? I do.";
"General: Comma-separated list of LastPass groups for the password manager to look in for passwords." = "General: Comma-separated list of LastPass groups for the password manager to look in for passwords.";
"General: Command to view man pages.\nUsed when you press the man page button on the touch bar. %@ is replaced with the command. End the command with & to avoid opening an iTerm2 window (e.g., if you're launching an external viewer)." = "General: Command to view man pages.\nUsed when you press the man page button on the touch bar. %@ is replaced with the command. End the command with & to avoid opening an iTerm2 window (e.g., if you're launching an external viewer).";
"General: Delay after changing number of screens/resolution until refresh (seconds).\nThis works around OS bugs where it takes some time after a screen change before it is safe to resize windows." = "General: Delay after changing number of screens/resolution until refresh (seconds).\nThis works around OS bugs where it takes some time after a screen change before it is safe to resize windows.";
"General: Delay between detecting a change to dynamic profiles and acting on it.\nIf a lot of changes happen to the DynamicProfiles folder a longer delay will help coalesce filesystem events to reduce CPU usage." = "General: Delay between detecting a change to dynamic profiles and acting on it.\nIf a lot of changes happen to the DynamicProfiles folder a longer delay will help coalesce filesystem events to reduce CPU usage.";
"General: Disable App Nap.\nChange effective after restarting iTerm2." = "General: Disable App Nap.\nChange effective after restarting iTerm2.";
"General: Disable DECRQCRA?\nThis control sequence allows an app running in the terminal to read its contents." = "General: Disable DECRQCRA?\nThis control sequence allows an app running in the terminal to read its contents.";
"General: Disable potentially insecure escape sequences.\nSome features of iTerm2 expand the surface area for security issues. Consider turning this on when viewing untrusted content. The following custom escape sequences will be disabled: RemoteHost, StealFocus, CurrentDir, SetProfile, CopyToClipboard, EndCopy, File, SetBackgroundImageFile, OSC 6’s proxy icon-changing feature. The following DEC sequences are disabled: DECRQCRA. The following xterm extensions are disabled: Window Title Reporting, Icon Title Reporting. This will break displaying inline images, file download, some shell integration features, and other features." = "General: Disable potentially insecure escape sequences.\nSome features of iTerm2 expand the surface area for security issues. Consider turning this on when viewing untrusted content. The following custom escape sequences will be disabled: RemoteHost, StealFocus, CurrentDir, SetProfile, CopyToClipboard, EndCopy, File, SetBackgroundImageFile, OSC 6’s proxy icon-changing feature. The following DEC sequences are disabled: DECRQCRA. The following xterm extensions are disabled: Window Title Reporting, Icon Title Reporting. This will break displaying inline images, file download, some shell integration features, and other features.";
"General: Disable remapping modifiers for system shortcuts.\nThis prevents asking for accessibility permission. It breaks remapping system shortcuts like cmd-tab." = "General: Disable remapping modifiers for system shortcuts.\nThis prevents asking for accessibility permission. It breaks remapping system shortcuts like cmd-tab.";
"General: Downloads folder.\nIf set, downloaded files go to this location instead of the user’s $HOME/Downloads folder." = "General: Downloads folder.\nIf set, downloaded files go to this location instead of the user’s $HOME/Downloads folder.";
"General: Dry-run “Erase All Settings and Data”.\nWhen enabled, the Erase All Settings and Data button logs what it would delete (via NSLog) instead of actually deleting anything, and does not quit. Intended for testing the feature." = "General: Dry-run “Erase All Settings and Data”.\nWhen enabled, the Erase All Settings and Data button logs what it would delete (via NSLog) instead of actually deleting anything, and does not quit. Intended for testing the feature.";
"General: Exclude utun interfaces from network utilization?\nThis is useful if you use a VPN and only want to see the traffic that goes over Wi-Fi or Ethernet." = "General: Exclude utun interfaces from network utilization?\nThis is useful if you use a VPN and only want to see the traffic that goes over Wi-Fi or Ethernet.";
"General: Folder for config files. There must not be a space in the path.\nIf empty, then ~/.config/iterm2 will be the default location." = "General: Folder for config files. There must not be a space in the path.\nIf empty, then ~/.config/iterm2 will be the default location.";
"General: Folder where the “Save” button in the screenshot window writes files.\nLeave empty to save to the Desktop. The “Save As…” button ignores this and always prompts for a location." = "General: Folder where the “Save” button in the screenshot window writes files.\nLeave empty to save to the Desktop. The “Save As…” button ignores this and always prompts for a location.";
"General: Grace period for automatic quitting after the last window is closed.\nIf iTerm2 is configured to quit automatically when the last window is closed, this setting gives a grace period (in seconds) after startup where that feature is disabled. Set to 0 to have no grace period." = "General: Grace period for automatic quitting after the last window is closed.\nIf iTerm2 is configured to quit automatically when the last window is closed, this setting gives a grace period (in seconds) after startup where that feature is disabled. Set to 0 to have no grace period.";
"General: Height of the status bar in points.\nThis will also affect the height of per-pane title bars becuase the status bar may be embedded in it. You must restart iTerm2 after changing this setting for it to take effect." = "General: Height of the status bar in points.\nThis will also affect the height of per-pane title bars becuase the status bar may be embedded in it. You must restart iTerm2 after changing this setting for it to take effect.";
"General: Hide stuck tooltips.\nWhen you hide iTerm2 using a hotkey while a tooltip is fading out it gets stuck because of an OS bug. Work around it with a nasty hack by enabling this feature." = "General: Hide stuck tooltips.\nWhen you hide iTerm2 using a hotkey while a tooltip is fading out it gets stuck because of an OS bug. Work around it with a nasty hack by enabling this feature.";
"General: Hotkey windows are excluded from Cycle Through Windows." = "General: Hotkey windows are excluded from Cycle Through Windows.";
"General: How long to wait for the emoji panel to open in seconds?\nFloating hotkey windows adjust their level when the emoji panel is open. If it’s really slow you might need to increase this value to prevent it from appearing beneath a floating hotkey window." = "General: How long to wait for the emoji panel to open in seconds?\nFloating hotkey windows adjust their level when the emoji panel is open. If it’s really slow you might need to increase this value to prevent it from appearing beneath a floating hotkey window.";
"General: Indicate the number of bells rung while the app is inactive in the dock icon’s badge label" = "General: Indicate the number of bells rung while the app is inactive in the dock icon’s badge label";
"General: LLM Platform.\nLegal values are: OpenAI, Azure, Gemini. This determines the format of requests and responses." = "General: LLM Platform.\nLegal values are: OpenAI, Azure, Gemini. This determines the format of requests and responses.";
"General: Maximum number of bytes of selection to provide to Python API.\nA large value here can cause performance issues when you have a big selection." = "General: Maximum number of bytes of selection to provide to Python API.\nA large value here can cause performance issues when you have a big selection.";
"General: Maximum number of bytes of selection to provide to Services.\nA large value here can cause performance issues when you have a big selection." = "General: Maximum number of bytes of selection to provide to Services.\nA large value here can cause performance issues when you have a big selection.";
"General: Maximum number of characters before and after the click location to search when applying word selection regex patterns." = "General: Maximum number of characters before and after the click location to search when applying word selection regex patterns.";
"General: Maximum number of lines before and after the click location to include in smart selection." = "General: Maximum number of lines before and after the click location to include in smart selection.";
"General: Maximum number of trigger-launched commands that can run at once.\nIf too many “Run Command…” triggers fire their commands will be queued. You must restart iTerm2 for changes to this setting to take effect." = "General: Maximum number of trigger-launched commands that can run at once.\nIf too many “Run Command…” triggers fire their commands will be queued. You must restart iTerm2 for changes to this setting to take effect.";
"General: Maximum pixel height for a single screenshot file.\nScreenshots taller than this will be split into multiple files. Also affects the maximum total pixels (this value squared / 5)." = "General: Maximum pixel height for a single screenshot file.\nScreenshots taller than this will be split into multiple files. Also affects the maximum total pixels (this value squared / 5).";
"General: Number of autocomplete options to present.\nA value less than 100 is recommended." = "General: Number of autocomplete options to present.\nA value less than 100 is recommended.";
"General: Omit session identifier from notifications.\nWhen enabled, notifications will only show the message without the session name and tab number prefix." = "General: Omit session identifier from notifications.\nWhen enabled, notifications will only show the message without the session name and tab number prefix.";
"General: Open a new window when you click the dock icon and no windows are already open, and also on app launch when no other windows are open?" = "General: Open a new window when you click the dock icon and no windows are already open, and also on app launch when no other windows are open?";
"General: Open a window at startup?\nThis is useful if you wish to use the system window restoration settings but not create a new window if none would be restored." = "General: Open a window at startup?\nThis is useful if you wish to use the system window restoration settings but not create a new window if none would be restored.";
"General: Path to folder with dynamic profiles.\nWhen empty, ~/Library/Application Support/iTerm2/DynamicProfiles will be used. You must restart iTerm2 after modifying this setting." = "General: Path to folder with dynamic profiles.\nWhen empty, ~/Library/Application Support/iTerm2/DynamicProfiles will be used. You must restart iTerm2 after modifying this setting.";
"General: Path to ftp for opening ftp: URLs.\nYou may want to set this to /usr/local/bin/ftp to use the Homebrew install." = "General: Path to ftp for opening ftp: URLs.\nYou may want to set this to /usr/local/bin/ftp to use the Homebrew install.";
"General: Path to telnet for opening telnet: URLs.\nYou may want to set this to /usr/local/bin/telnet to use the Homebrew install." = "General: Path to telnet for opening telnet: URLs.\nYou may want to set this to /usr/local/bin/telnet to use the Homebrew install.";
"General: Perform dictionary lookups on force press.\nIf this is NO, force press will still preview the Semantic History action; only dictionary lookups can be disabled." = "General: Perform dictionary lookups on force press.\nIf this is NO, force press will still preview the Semantic History action; only dictionary lookups can be disabled.";
"General: Perform restorable state integrity checks?" = "General: Perform restorable state integrity checks?";
"General: Pin Edit Session window to the session it originally edited.\nIf not set, it will affect the most recently active session." = "General: Pin Edit Session window to the session it originally edited.\nIf not set, it will affect the most recently active session.";
"General: Rate limit for Alert triggers.\nIf the same trigger fires with less than this time interval (in seconds) between firings, it will be suppressed." = "General: Rate limit for Alert triggers.\nIf the same trigger fires with less than this time interval (in seconds) between firings, it will be suppressed.";
"General: Rate limit for Notification triggers.\nIf the same trigger fires with less than this time interval (in seconds) between firings, it will be suppressed." = "General: Rate limit for Notification triggers.\nIf the same trigger fires with less than this time interval (in seconds) between firings, it will be suppressed.";
"General: Redraw the screen after the Clear Buffer menu item is selected.\nWhen enabled, the TTY size is briefly changed after clearing the buffer to cause the shell or current app to redraw." = "General: Redraw the screen after the Clear Buffer menu item is selected.\nWhen enabled, the TTY size is briefly changed after clearing the buffer to cause the shell or current app to redraw.";
"General: Relay origin for companion iOS device pairing.\nMust be a bare https origin (scheme and host, no path), such as https://companion-relay.iterm2.com. The relay is the only transport, so this must be set for pairing to work; forks can point it at their own Worker. Leave empty to disable the relay entirely. The user defaults key is `CompanionRelayOrigin`." = "General: Relay origin for companion iOS device pairing.\nMust be a bare https origin (scheme and host, no path), such as https://companion-relay.iterm2.com. The relay is the only transport, so this must be set for pairing to work; forks can point it at their own Worker. Leave empty to disable the relay entirely. The user defaults key is `CompanionRelayOrigin`.";
"General: Reveal file created by “Export All Settings and Data” in finder upon completion" = "General: Reveal file created by “Export All Settings and Data” in finder upon completion";
"General: Save scroll buffer when clearing screen.\nWhen enabled, saves the current screen into scroll back buffer instead of clearing it." = "General: Save scroll buffer when clearing screen.\nWhen enabled, saves the current screen into scroll back buffer instead of clearing it.";
"General: Save the screen to scrollback when an app moves the cursor above the prompt.\nSome full-screen programs that don’t use the alternate screen buffer repaint by moving the cursor to the top of the screen and overwriting whatever was already there, destroying content you can still see. When enabled, iTerm2 first scrolls the visible screen into history so that content isn’t lost. Requires shell integration." = "General: Save the screen to scrollback when an app moves the cursor above the prompt.\nSome full-screen programs that don’t use the alternate screen buffer repaint by moving the cursor to the top of the screen and overwriting whatever was already there, destroying content you can still see. When enabled, iTerm2 first scrolls the visible screen into history so that content isn’t lost. Requires shell integration.";
"General: Shard-map URL for companion iOS device pairing.\nAn https URL pointing directly at the static shard-map JSON, used to find the relay shard that serves the phone-to-mac connection. It is fetched verbatim (nothing is appended). Leave empty to use direct connections (such as if you run your own relay)." = "General: Shard-map URL for companion iOS device pairing.\nAn https URL pointing directly at the static shard-map JSON, used to find the relay shard that serves the phone-to-mac connection. It is fetched verbatim (nothing is appended). Leave empty to use direct connections (such as if you run your own relay).";
"General: Should opening a script with iTerm2 disable the default profile's “Send Text at Start” setting?\nIf you use “open iTerm2 file.command” or drag a script onto iTerm2's icon and this setting is enabled then the script will be executed in lieu of the profile's “Send Text at Start” setting. If this setting is off then both will be executed." = "General: Should opening a script with iTerm2 disable the default profile's “Send Text at Start” setting?\nIf you use “open iTerm2 file.command” or drag a script onto iTerm2's icon and this setting is enabled then the script will be executed in lieu of the profile's “Send Text at Start” setting. If this setting is off then both will be executed.";
"General: Should split pane navigation by direction wrap around?" = "General: Should split pane navigation by direction wrap around?";
"General: Show buttons at the top of a selected command?\nWhen you select a command by single clicking the command line or its output, buttons are shown on the top right with options like Copy and Share. Note that this setting only applies when marks are not “line style” such as when using Auto Composer." = "General: Show buttons at the top of a selected command?\nWhen you select a command by single clicking the command line or its output, buttons are shown on the top right with options like Copy and Share. Note that this setting only applies when marks are not “line style” such as when using Auto Composer.";
"General: Show hints in split pane menu items to indicate horizontal vs vertical semantics.\nYou must restart iTerm2 after changing this setting for it to take effect." = "General: Show hints in split pane menu items to indicate horizontal vs vertical semantics.\nYou must restart iTerm2 after changing this setting for it to take effect.";
"General: Suppress confirmation of terminal-initiated downloads?" = "General: Suppress confirmation of terminal-initiated downloads?";
"General: Swap Find Next and Find Previous.\nIf enabled, Find Next will search up and Find Previous will search down (iTerm2's traditional behavior, which is a departure from macOS's standard). When disabled, search behaves like a normal macOS app." = "General: Swap Find Next and Find Previous.\nIf enabled, Find Next will search up and Find Previous will search down (iTerm2's traditional behavior, which is a departure from macOS's standard). When disabled, search behaves like a normal macOS app.";
"General: Synchronize search queries across windows and applications.\nNormally, when you enter a search query in a Find field all find fields in all applications get updated to hold the same value. This is utter nonsense, and can be disabled by setting this preference to No." = "General: Synchronize search queries across windows and applications.\nNormally, when you enter a search query in a Find field all find fields in all applications get updated to hold the same value. This is utter nonsense, and can be disabled by setting this preference to No.";
"General: System notifications should be silent." = "General: System notifications should be silent.";
"General: Template for URL of search engine.\niTerm2 replaces the string “%@” with the text to search for. Query parameter percent escaping is used." = "General: Template for URL of search engine.\niTerm2 replaces the string “%@” with the text to search for. Query parameter percent escaping is used.";
"General: Template of URL for typeahead search suggestions.\niTerm replaces the string “%@” with the text to search for. Query parameter percent escaping is used." = "General: Template of URL for typeahead search suggestions.\niTerm replaces the string “%@” with the text to search for. Query parameter percent escaping is used.";
"General: Time in seconds before a session is considered idle.\nUsed for updating icons and activity indicator in tabs." = "General: Time in seconds before a session is considered idle.\nUsed for updating icons and activity indicator in tabs.";
"General: Time to wait before performing Find action on 1- or 2- character queries." = "General: Time to wait before performing Find action on 1- or 2- character queries.";
"General: Time to wait before showing tips in the main menu.\nSet this to a big number if you don’t like the tips." = "General: Time to wait before showing tips in the main menu.\nSet this to a big number if you don’t like the tips.";
"General: Timeout (seconds) for evaluating RPCs.\nThis applies to invoking functions registered by scripts when using the Swift syntax for inline expressions." = "General: Timeout (seconds) for evaluating RPCs.\nThis applies to invoking functions registered by scripts when using the Swift syntax for inline expressions.";
"General: Timeout for downloading settings" = "General: Timeout for downloading settings";
"General: Timeout in seconds when running git for the status bar component." = "General: Timeout in seconds when running git for the status bar component.";
"General: Treat the top row of keys like number keys on an English keyboard for the purposes of switching panes, tabs, and windows with modifier+number.\nFor example, AZERTY requires you to hold down Shift to enter a number. To switch tabs with ⌘+Number on an AZERTY keyboard, you must enable this setting. Then, for example, ⌘-& switches to tab 1. When this setting is enabled, some user-defined shortcuts may become unavailable because the tab/window/pane switching behavior takes precedence." = "General: Treat the top row of keys like number keys on an English keyboard for the purposes of switching panes, tabs, and windows with modifier+number.\nFor example, AZERTY requires you to hold down Shift to enter a number. To switch tabs with ⌘+Number on an AZERTY keyboard, you must enable this setting. Then, for example, ⌘-& switches to tab 1. When this setting is enabled, some user-defined shortcuts may become unavailable because the tab/window/pane switching behavior takes precedence.";
"General: URL to check for updates to the AI model catalog.\nThe catalog defines the built-in AI models (context window, capabilities, and the recommended model per vendor). iTerm2 periodically downloads a signed newer copy so new models become available without an app update. This happens only when AI features are enabled and you have granted permission; a non-empty URL by itself does not enable checking. Clearing this URL disables checking entirely." = "General: URL to check for updates to the AI model catalog.\nThe catalog defines the built-in AI models (context window, capabilities, and the recommended model per vendor). iTerm2 periodically downloads a signed newer copy so new models become available without an app update. This happens only when AI features are enabled and you have granted permission; a non-empty URL by itself does not enable checking. Clearing this URL disables checking entirely.";
"General: Use Open Directory to determine the user shell" = "General: Use Open Directory to determine the user shell";
"General: Use old-style find and paste progress indicator views.\nThis change will only affect new windows." = "General: Use old-style find and paste progress indicator views.\nThis change will only affect new windows.";
"General: User agent for web views. Leave empty to use system default." = "General: User agent for web views. Leave empty to use system default.";
"General: Value to set LC_CTYPE to if the machine‘s combination of country and language are not supported.\nIf unset, the encoding (e.g., UTF-8) will be used." = "General: Value to set LC_CTYPE to if the machine‘s combination of country and language are not supported.\nIf unset, the encoding (e.g., UTF-8) will be used.";
"General: When sorting command history for auto command completion: how much should number of uses of a command contribute to its score? A higher score moves the command closer to the top of the list.\nUse 0 to ignore number of uses." = "General: When sorting command history for auto command completion: how much should number of uses of a command contribute to its score? A higher score moves the command closer to the top of the list.\nUse 0 to ignore number of uses.";
"General: When sorting command history for auto command completion: how much should the time-since-last-use of a command contribute to its score? A higher score moves the command closer to the top of the list.\nUse 0 to ignore time since last use." = "General: When sorting command history for auto command completion: how much should the time-since-last-use of a command contribute to its score? A higher score moves the command closer to the top of the list.\nUse 0 to ignore time since last use.";
