"Tabs: Allow two-finger interactive swipe between tabs?\nThe system preference Trackpad > More Gestures > Swipe between pages controls this globally. When “swipe with two fingers” is enabled, you can change this setting to “No” to prevent swiping between tabs in iTerm2." = "Tabs: Allow two-finger interactive swipe between tabs?\nThe system preference Trackpad > More Gestures > Swipe between pages controls this globally. When “swipe with two fingers” is enabled, you can change this setting to “No” to prevent swiping between tabs in iTerm2.";
"Tabs: Alpha value for tab color for non-selected colored tabs in the Minimal theme.\nMust be between 0 and 1." = "Tabs: Alpha value for tab color for non-selected colored tabs in the Minimal theme.\nMust be between 0 and 1.";
"Tabs: Animation duration for fade in/out animation of tabs in full screen, in seconds." = "Tabs: Animation duration for fade in/out animation of tabs in full screen, in seconds.";
"Tabs: Choosing a profile from the “Profiles” menu opens a new window.\nYou must restart iTerm2 after changing this setting for it to take effect." = "Tabs: Choosing a profile from the “Profiles” menu opens a new window.\nYou must restart iTerm2 after changing this setting for it to take effect.";
"Tabs: Color of drop target fill when dragging a split pane.\nShould be a web-style color, #rrggbb. You can also use p3#rrggbb for p3 color space." = "Tabs: Color of drop target fill when dragging a split pane.\nShould be a web-style color, #rrggbb. You can also use p3#rrggbb for p3 color space.";
"Tabs: Color of drop target inner border when dragging a split pane.\nShould be a web-style color, #rrggbb. You can also use p3#rrggbb for p3 color space." = "Tabs: Color of drop target inner border when dragging a split pane.\nShould be a web-style color, #rrggbb. You can also use p3#rrggbb for p3 color space.";
"Tabs: Color of drop target outer border when dragging a split pane.\nShould be a web-style color, #rrggbb. You can also use p3#rrggbb for p3 color space." = "Tabs: Color of drop target outer border when dragging a split pane.\nShould be a web-style color, #rrggbb. You can also use p3#rrggbb for p3 color space.";
"Tabs: Color of source pane fill when moving/swapping a split pane.\nShould be a web-style color, #rrggbb. You can also use p3#rrggbb for p3 color space." = "Tabs: Color of source pane fill when moving/swapping a split pane.\nShould be a web-style color, #rrggbb. You can also use p3#rrggbb for p3 color space.";
"Tabs: Color of source pane inner border when moving/swapping a split pane.\nShould be a web-style color, #rrggbb. You can also use p3#rrggbb for p3 color space." = "Tabs: Color of source pane inner border when moving/swapping a split pane.\nShould be a web-style color, #rrggbb. You can also use p3#rrggbb for p3 color space.";
"Tabs: Color of source pane outer border when moving/swapping a split pane.\nShould be a web-style color, #rrggbb. You can also use p3#rrggbb for p3 color space." = "Tabs: Color of source pane outer border when moving/swapping a split pane.\nShould be a web-style color, #rrggbb. You can also use p3#rrggbb for p3 color space.";
"Tabs: Colors for tab color menu item.\nSpace delimited strings like #rrggbb or #rgb in sRGB color space. If the P3 color space is available, you can use strings like: color(p3 1 0.5 0.25)" = "Tabs: Colors for tab color menu item.\nSpace delimited strings like #rrggbb or #rgb in sRGB color space. If the P3 color space is available, you can use strings like: color(p3 1 0.5 0.25)";
"Tabs: Custom tab label font size\nFor this to take effect, turn on “Use custom font size for tab labels?”." = "Tabs: Custom tab label font size\nFor this to take effect, turn on “Use custom font size for tab labels?”.";
"Tabs: Default tab bar height\nThis does not affect the minimal or compact themes. On macOS 26 Tahoe-style tabs, the top (horizontal) tab bar uses the system height and ignores this setting; left/right (vertical) tabs use max(26, this value) for each tab’s height." = "Tabs: Default tab bar height\nThis does not affect the minimal or compact themes. On macOS 26 Tahoe-style tabs, the top (horizontal) tab bar uses the system height and ignores this setting; left/right (vertical) tabs use max(26, this value) for each tab’s height.";
"Tabs: Disable tab bar tooltips?" = "Tabs: Disable tab bar tooltips?";
"Tabs: Draw bottom line for horizontal tabbar in Regular, Dark and Light theme?" = "Tabs: Draw bottom line for horizontal tabbar in Regular, Dark and Light theme?";
"Tabs: High Contrast modes maximize visibility.\nWhen enabled, the dark high-contrast theme emphasizes visibility over beauty." = "Tabs: High Contrast modes maximize visibility.\nWhen enabled, the dark high-contrast theme emphasizes visibility over beauty.";
"Tabs: How far must the mouse move before a tab drag is initiated?\nYou must restart iTerm2 after changing this setting for it to take effect." = "Tabs: How far must the mouse move before a tab drag is initiated?\nYou must restart iTerm2 after changing this setting for it to take effect.";
"Tabs: How long in seconds to show tabs in fullscreen.\nThe tab bar appears briefly in fullscreen when the number of tabs changes or you switch tabs. This setting gives the time in seconds for it to remain visible." = "Tabs: How long in seconds to show tabs in fullscreen.\nThe tab bar appears briefly in fullscreen when the number of tabs changes or you switch tabs. This setting gives the time in seconds for it to remain visible.";
"Tabs: How much should contrast be increased for text in tabs in the Minimal theme?\nChoose a value larger than 1 to increase contrast. Values between 0 and 1 have less contrast than the default." = "Tabs: How much should contrast be increased for text in tabs in the Minimal theme?\nChoose a value larger than 1 to increase contrast. Values between 0 and 1 have less contrast than the default.";
"Tabs: How prominent should the outline around the selected tab be drawn when there are colored tabs in a window?\nTakes a value in 0 to 3, where 0 means no outline and 3 means a very prominent outline." = "Tabs: How prominent should the outline around the selected tab be drawn when there are colored tabs in a window?\nTakes a value in 0 to 3, where 0 means no outline and 3 means a very prominent outline.";
"Tabs: How prominent should the text in a non-selected tab be when there are colored tabs in a window?\nTakes a value in 0 to 1, the alpha value." = "Tabs: How prominent should the text in a non-selected tab be when there are colored tabs in a window?\nTakes a value in 0 to 1, the alpha value.";
"Tabs: Ignore System Settings > Dock > Prefer tabs when opening documents?\nWhen set to No, asking to open a window will open a tab instead when system settings is configured to prefer tabs over windows. When set to Yes, asking to open a window may open a tab instead." = "Tabs: Ignore System Settings > Dock > Prefer tabs when opening documents?\nWhen set to No, asking to open a window will open a tab instead when system settings is configured to prefer tabs over windows. When set to Yes, asking to open a window may open a tab instead.";
"Tabs: In the Compact theme, you can move the window by dragging starting in a region on the edge near the window border. This gives the size of that region." = "Tabs: In the Compact theme, you can move the window by dragging starting in a region on the edge near the window border. This gives the size of that region.";
"Tabs: In the Minimal and Compact themes when there is a single tab and the tab bar is visible, should dragging the tab bar move the window?\nThis also affects windows without titlebars in any theme." = "Tabs: In the Minimal and Compact themes when there is a single tab and the tab bar is visible, should dragging the tab bar move the window?\nThis also affects windows without titlebars in any theme.";
"Tabs: In the Minimal theme, how different should the background color of the selected tab be from the others?\nTakes a value in 0 to 1, where 0 is no difference and 1 very different." = "Tabs: In the Minimal theme, how different should the background color of the selected tab be from the others?\nTakes a value in 0 to 1, where 0 is no difference and 1 very different.";
"Tabs: In the Minimal theme, how prominent should split pane dividers be?\nTakes a value in 0 to 1, where 0 is invisible and 1 is very prominent" = "Tabs: In the Minimal theme, how prominent should split pane dividers be?\nTakes a value in 0 to 1, where 0 is invisible and 1 is very prominent";
"Tabs: In the Minimal theme, how prominent should the tab outline be?\nTakes a value in 0 to 1, where 0 is invisible and 1 is very prominent" = "Tabs: In the Minimal theme, how prominent should the tab outline be?\nTakes a value in 0 to 1, where 0 is invisible and 1 is very prominent";
"Tabs: In the Minimal theme, should the area left of the tab bar be treated as part of the first tab?" = "Tabs: In the Minimal theme, should the area left of the tab bar be treated as part of the first tab?";
"Tabs: In the Minimal theme, you can move the window by dragging starting in a region on the edge near the window border. This gives the size of that region." = "Tabs: In the Minimal theme, you can move the window by dragging starting in a region on the edge near the window border. This gives the size of that region.";
"Tabs: Minimum tab width when using uneven tab widths for compact tabs." = "Tabs: Minimum tab width when using uneven tab widths for compact tabs.";
"Tabs: Minimum tab width when using uneven tab widths." = "Tabs: Minimum tab width when using uneven tab widths.";
"Tabs: Minimum width for tab labels.\nThe activity/bell icon will be hidden when the space for the label drops below this size (in points)" = "Tabs: Minimum width for tab labels.\nThe activity/bell icon will be hidden when the space for the label drops below this size (in points)";
"Tabs: Next Pane and Previous Pane commands use reading order, not the time of last use." = "Tabs: Next Pane and Previous Pane commands use reading order, not the time of last use.";
"Tabs: Place the tabbar in the window's titlebar in full screen mode (macOS 13+ only)?\nThis can be disabled to work around a bug in macOS where tabs may not be visible in full screen." = "Tabs: Place the tabbar in the window's titlebar in full screen mode (macOS 13+ only)?\nThis can be disabled to work around a bug in macOS where tabs may not be visible in full screen.";
"Tabs: Preferred tab width when tabs are equally sized." = "Tabs: Preferred tab width when tabs are equally sized.";
"Tabs: Prominence of selected tab underline indicator in the Minimal theme when there is at least one colored tab." = "Tabs: Prominence of selected tab underline indicator in the Minimal theme when there is at least one colored tab.";
"Tabs: Remove the “new tab” button from horizontal tab bars?" = "Tabs: Remove the “new tab” button from horizontal tab bars?";
"Tabs: Select tabs on mouse-down?\nChanging this setting will not affect existing windows." = "Tabs: Select tabs on mouse-down?\nChanging this setting will not affect existing windows.";
"Tabs: Select the tab to the left when closing a tab?\nIf disabled, the tab to the right of the closing tab will be selected." = "Tabs: Select the tab to the left when closing a tab?\nIf disabled, the tab to the right of the closing tab will be selected.";
"Tabs: Should double-clicking a tab open a window to edit its title?" = "Tabs: Should double-clicking a tab open a window to edit its title?";
"Tabs: Should middle-click on a tab in the tab bar close the tab?" = "Tabs: Should middle-click on a tab in the tab bar close the tab?";
"Tabs: Should tab close buttons always remain visible?" = "Tabs: Should tab close buttons always remain visible?";
"Tabs: Should the “new tab” button in the tab bar use the current session’s profile?\nWhen enabled, clicking the “+” button opens a new tab with the current session’s profile instead of the default profile." = "Tabs: Should the “new tab” button in the tab bar use the current session’s profile?\nWhen enabled, clicking the “+” button opens a new tab with the current session’s profile instead of the default profile.";
"Tabs: Tab bar height (points) for the Minimal theme.\nThe default is 38. Use 22 to match the compact theme's height." = "Tabs: Tab bar height (points) for the Minimal theme.\nThe default is 38. Use 22 to match the compact theme's height.";
"Tabs: Tab width when the tab bar is scrollable.\nUsed as the fixed width when tabs are equally sized, and as the minimum width when uneven tab widths are allowed." = "Tabs: Tab width when the tab bar is scrollable.\nUsed as the fixed width when tabs are equally sized, and as the minimum width when uneven tab widths are allowed.";
"Tabs: Uneven tab widths allowed." = "Tabs: Uneven tab widths allowed.";
"Tabs: Use Sequoia-style tabs in Tahoe and later?" = "Tabs: Use Sequoia-style tabs in Tahoe and later?";
"Tabs: Use custom font size for tab labels?\nSee also advanced setting “Custom tab label font size”." = "Tabs: Use custom font size for tab labels?\nSee also advanced setting “Custom tab label font size”.";
"Tabs: Use the running command's first letter as the tab's default icon if there isn't a built in one.\nThis takes effect when tabs are configured to use built-in icons." = "Tabs: Use the running command's first letter as the tab's default icon if there isn't a built in one.\nThis takes effect when tabs are configured to use built-in icons.";
"Tabs: Use “smart truncation” for tab titles.\nIf a tab‘s title is too long to fit, ellipsize the start of the title if more tabs have unique suffixes than prefixes in a given window." = "Tabs: Use “smart truncation” for tab titles.\nIf a tab‘s title is too long to fit, ellipsize the start of the title if more tabs have unique suffixes than prefixes in a given window.";
"Tabs: Width of pinned tabs in pixels." = "Tabs: Width of pinned tabs in pixels.";
"Tags for organizing and filtering profiles" = "Tags for organizing and filtering profiles";
"Tags to filter available snippets" = "Tags to filter available snippets";
"Template for log filename" = "Template for log filename";
"Terminal background color" = "Terminal background color";
"Terminal background color in dark mode" = "Terminal background color in dark mode";
"Terminal background color in light mode" = "Terminal background color in light mode";
"Terminal type string reported to applications (e.g., xterm-256color)" = "Terminal type string reported to applications (e.g., xterm-256color)";
"Terminal: Accept OSC 7 to set username, hostname, and path." = "Terminal: Accept OSC 7 to set username, hostname, and path.";
"Terminal: Amount of time to wait while testing if echo is on (seconds).\nThis is used by the password manager to ensure you're at a password prompt. Set to 0 to disable echo probe." = "Terminal: Amount of time to wait while testing if echo is on (seconds).\nThis is used by the password manager to ensure you're at a password prompt. Set to 0 to disable echo probe.";
"Terminal: Apps may turn on Focus Reporting.\nFocus reporting causes iTerm2 to send an escape sequence when a session gains or loses focus. It can cause problems when an ssh session dies unexpectedly because it gets left on, so some users prefer to disable it." = "Terminal: Apps may turn on Focus Reporting.\nFocus reporting causes iTerm2 to send an escape sequence when a session gains or loses focus. It can cause problems when an ssh session dies unexpectedly because it gets left on, so some users prefer to disable it.";
"Terminal: Automatically enable secure keyboard entry at password prompts?" = "Terminal: Automatically enable secure keyboard entry at password prompts?";
"Terminal: Automatically silence bell when it rings too much." = "Terminal: Automatically silence bell when it rings too much.";
"Terminal: Bounce dock icon when the bell rings while another app is active?" = "Terminal: Bounce dock icon when the bell rings while another app is active?";
"Terminal: Command to run when handling an ssh:// URL." = "Terminal: Command to run when handling an ssh:// URL.";
"Terminal: Convert italics to reverse video in tmux integration, even when TERM matches *tmux*?\nThis was the default behavior for a long time, but it was incorrect. The conversion should only be done when TERM matches *screen*." = "Terminal: Convert italics to reverse video in tmux integration, even when TERM matches *tmux*?\nThis was the default behavior for a long time, but it was incorrect. The conversion should only be done when TERM matches *screen*.";
"Terminal: Convert italics to reverse video in tmux integration?\nThis is effective when the default TERM reported by tmux matches *screen*." = "Terminal: Convert italics to reverse video in tmux integration?\nThis is effective when the default TERM reported by tmux matches *screen*.";
"Terminal: Cursor blink speed (seconds)." = "Terminal: Cursor blink speed (seconds).";
"Terminal: Cursor occupies line spacing area.\nIf lines have more than 100% vertical spacing and this setting is enabled the bottom of the cursor will be aligned to the bottom of the spacing area." = "Terminal: Cursor occupies line spacing area.\nIf lines have more than 100% vertical spacing and this setting is enabled the bottom of the cursor will be aligned to the bottom of the spacing area.";
"Terminal: Debug: highlight prompt mark prompt/command/excluded ranges in the legacy (non-GPU) renderer.\nWhen enabled, the legacy renderer overlays a blue outline around each visible prompt mark’s prompt range (OSC 133 A to B), a green outline around its command range (B to C), and a red outline around each excluded subrange (PS2 prefixes and right-prompt regions recorded via OSC 133 k=). Disable the Metal renderer (Settings → General → Magic) to see this. Intended for development and bug reports; leave off in normal use." = "Terminal: Debug: highlight prompt mark prompt/command/excluded ranges in the legacy (non-GPU) renderer.\nWhen enabled, the legacy renderer overlays a blue outline around each visible prompt mark’s prompt range (OSC 133 A to B), a green outline around its command range (B to C), and a red outline around each excluded subrange (PS2 prefixes and right-prompt regions recorded via OSC 133 k=). Disable the Metal renderer (Settings → General → Magic) to see this. Intended for development and bug reports; leave off in normal use.";
"Terminal: Default tab stop width for new sessions.\nNote: this will break drawing in emacs and other apps." = "Terminal: Default tab stop width for new sessions.\nNote: this will break drawing in emacs and other apps.";
"Terminal: Disable animations for showing/hiding password manager." = "Terminal: Disable animations for showing/hiding password manager.";
"Terminal: Evaluate idempotent triggers periodically in interactive apps, even when triggers in interactive apps are disabled." = "Terminal: Evaluate idempotent triggers periodically in interactive apps, even when triggers in interactive apps are disabled.";
"Terminal: How long (seconds) terminal echo must remain disabled before iTerm2 treats it as a password prompt.\nThis prevents shell scripts that briefly turn off echo (e.g. while reading the response to an OSC report request) from triggering the password manager. Set to 0 to disable debouncing." = "Terminal: How long (seconds) terminal echo must remain disabled before iTerm2 treats it as a password prompt.\nThis prevents shell scripts that briefly turn off echo (e.g. while reading the response to an OSC report request) from triggering the password manager. Set to 0 to disable debouncing.";
"Terminal: Initial alpha value when flashing the visual bell or search wraparound indicator" = "Terminal: Initial alpha value when flashing the visual bell or search wraparound indicator";
"Terminal: Maximum length for OSC 8 URLs" = "Terminal: Maximum length for OSC 8 URLs";
"Terminal: Maximum number of chunks to buffer.\nIn general, these chunks are 1024 bytes. A larger value increases buffer bloat but—up to a limit—can improve performance in the fast path of ASCII text." = "Terminal: Maximum number of chunks to buffer.\nIn general, these chunks are 1024 bytes. A larger value increases buffer bloat but—up to a limit—can improve performance in the fast path of ASCII text.";
"Terminal: Maximum number of lines of history to expose to Accessibility.\nAccessibility APIs can make iTerm2 slow. In order to limit the effect, you can restrict the number of lines in each session that are visible to accessibility. The last lines of each session will be made accessible." = "Terminal: Maximum number of lines of history to expose to Accessibility.\nAccessibility APIs can make iTerm2 slow. In order to limit the effect, you can restrict the number of lines in each session that are visible to accessibility. The last lines of each session will be made accessible.";
"Terminal: Maximum number of lines of history to restore.\nWhen the app is relaunched, only the last N lines of history are restored to avoid making launch too slow. If you reduce this number, existing sessions won't be affected until their history is cleared." = "Terminal: Maximum number of lines of history to restore.\nWhen the app is relaunched, only the last N lines of history are restored to avoid making launch too slow. If you reduce this number, existing sessions won't be affected until their history is cleared.";
"Terminal: Minimum time between beeping or flashing screen on bell, in seconds.\nIf the time interval between bells is less than this amount of time, it will be ignored." = "Terminal: Minimum time between beeping or flashing screen on bell, in seconds.\nIf the time interval between bells is less than this amount of time, it will be ignored.";
"Terminal: Never set the CTYPE environment variable." = "Terminal: Never set the CTYPE environment variable.";
"Terminal: Number of screen lines to match against trigger regular expressions.\nTrigger regular expressions are matched against the last logical line of text when a newline is received. A search is performed to find the start of the line. Since very long lines would cause performance problems, the search (and consequently the regular expression match, highlighting, and so on) is limited to this many screen lines." = "Terminal: Number of screen lines to match against trigger regular expressions.\nTrigger regular expressions are matched against the last logical line of text when a newline is received. A search is performed to find the start of the line. Since very long lines would cause performance problems, the search (and consequently the regular expression match, highlighting, and so on) is limited to this many screen lines.";
"Terminal: Prevent CSI 3 J from clearing scrollback history?\nThis is also known as the terminfo E3 capability." = "Terminal: Prevent CSI 3 J from clearing scrollback history?\nThis is also known as the terminfo E3 capability.";
"Terminal: Prevent control sequences from changing the current profile?" = "Terminal: Prevent control sequences from changing the current profile?";
"Terminal: Regular expression for “Find URLs” command." = "Terminal: Regular expression for “Find URLs” command.";
"Terminal: Restore window contents at startup.\nThis requires “System Settings > Desktop & Dock > Close windows when quitting an app” to be off." = "Terminal: Restore window contents at startup.\nThis requires “System Settings > Desktop & Dock > Close windows when quitting an app” to be off.";
"Terminal: Set $TERMINFO_DIRS to add modern terminal features to xterm-like $TERMs?\niTerm2 ships with extended terminfo capabilities for common TERMs (xterm, xterm-new, and xterm-256color). For example, it enables undercurl. New sessions get created with a TERMINFO_DIRS that make the customized TERMINFOs take precedence over the system defaults." = "Terminal: Set $TERMINFO_DIRS to add modern terminal features to xterm-like $TERMs?\niTerm2 ships with extended terminfo capabilities for common TERMs (xterm, xterm-new, and xterm-256color). For example, it enables undercurl. New sessions get created with a TERMINFO_DIRS that make the customized TERMINFOs take precedence over the system defaults.";
"Terminal: Show key at cursor at password prompt?" = "Terminal: Show key at cursor at password prompt?";
"Terminal: Support TERM=screen\nMost notably, this fixes italics replacing inverse text." = "Terminal: Support TERM=screen\nMost notably, this fixes italics replacing inverse text.";
"Terminal: Tabs wrap around to the next line.\nThis is useful for preserving tabs for later copying to the pasteboard. It breaks backward compatibility and may cause layout problems with programs that don’t expect this behavior." = "Terminal: Tabs wrap around to the next line.\nThis is useful for preserving tabs for later copying to the pasteboard. It breaks backward compatibility and may cause layout problems with programs that don’t expect this behavior.";
"Terminal: Threshold for Smart Cursor Color for background color (0 to 1).\n0 means the cursor’s background color will always be the cell’s text color, while 1 means it will always be black or white." = "Terminal: Threshold for Smart Cursor Color for background color (0 to 1).\n0 means the cursor’s background color will always be the cell’s text color, while 1 means it will always be black or white.";
"Terminal: Threshold for Smart Cursor Color for text color (0 to 1).\n0 means the cursor’s text color will always be the cell’s background color, while 1 means it will always be black or white." = "Terminal: Threshold for Smart Cursor Color for text color (0 to 1).\n0 means the cursor’s text color will always be the cell’s background color, while 1 means it will always be black or white.";
"Terminal: To drag images or selected text, you must hold ⌘. This prevents accidental drags." = "Terminal: To drag images or selected text, you must hold ⌘. This prevents accidental drags.";
"Terminal: Use P3 as default color space? If No, sRGB will be used." = "Terminal: Use P3 as default color space? If No, sRGB will be used.";
"Terminal: Use fallback for COLORFGBG if no exact match found?\nThe COLORFGBG variable indicates the ANSI colors that match the foreground and background colors. If no colors match and this setting is enabled, then the variable will be set to 15;0 to indicate a dark background or 0;15 to indicate a light background." = "Terminal: Use fallback for COLORFGBG if no exact match found?\nThe COLORFGBG variable indicates the ANSI colors that match the foreground and background colors. If no colors match and this setting is enabled, then the variable will be set to 15;0 to indicate a dark background or 0;15 to indicate a light background.";
"Terminal: Variables to report via control sequence\nThis is a comma-delimited list of variables that can be reported with the OSC 1337 ReportVariable=name control sequence. Each variable name must be prefixed with “allow:” or “deny:”." = "Terminal: Variables to report via control sequence\nThis is a comma-delimited list of variables that can be reported with the OSC 1337 ReportVariable=name control sequence. Each variable name must be prefixed with “allow:” or “deny:”.";
"Terminal: Vertical offset for underline cursor.\nPositive values move it up, negative values move it down." = "Terminal: Vertical offset for underline cursor.\nPositive values move it up, negative values move it down.";
"Terminal: Visual bell flashes the whole screen, not just a bell icon." = "Terminal: Visual bell flashes the whole screen, not just a bell icon.";
"Terminal: Warn if the `open` command appears to fail when secure keyboard input is enabled?" = "Terminal: Warn if the `open` command appears to fail when secure keyboard input is enabled?";
"Terminal: When evaluating idempotent triggers in interactive apps, wait this long (in seconds) between updates.\nThis limits the performance impact of trigger evaluation." = "Terminal: When evaluating idempotent triggers in interactive apps, wait this long (in seconds) between updates.\nThis limits the performance impact of trigger evaluation.";
"Terminal: When files are dropped into a terminal window, execute a silent coprocess.\nThis is an interpolated string. Use \\(filenames) to reference the shell-quoted, space-delimited full paths to the dropped files. If this preference is empty, the filenames get pasted instead." = "Terminal: When files are dropped into a terminal window, execute a silent coprocess.\nThis is an interpolated string. Use \\(filenames) to reference the shell-quoted, space-delimited full paths to the dropped files. If this preference is empty, the filenames get pasted instead.";
"Terminal: When rendering natively, use wide mode by default?" = "Terminal: When rendering natively, use wide mode by default?";
"Terminal: When using “Find URLs”, extend results across soft boundaries like tmux pane dividers." = "Terminal: When using “Find URLs”, extend results across soft boundaries like tmux pane dividers.";
"Terminal: Width of vertical bar cursor." = "Terminal: Width of vertical bar cursor.";
"Terminal: Zero-Width Space (U+200B) advances cursor?\nWhile a zero-width space should not advance the cursor per the Unicode spec, both Terminal.app and Konsole do this, and Weechat depends on it. You must restart iTerm2 after changing this setting." = "Terminal: Zero-Width Space (U+200B) advances cursor?\nWhile a zero-width space should not advance the cursor per the Unicode spec, both Terminal.app and Konsole do this, and Weechat depends on it. You must restart iTerm2 after changing this setting.";
"Terminal: xterm version for secondary device attributes (SDA).\nIncreasing this number enables more features in apps but may break things. Use 95 to recover pre-3.4.10 behavior." = "Terminal: xterm version for secondary device attributes (SDA).\nIncreasing this number enables more features in apps but may break things. Use 95 to recover pre-3.4.10 behavior.";
