"Some keyboard layouts (such as AZERTY) require a modifier to press a number key. This causes problems for switching to a window, tab, or split pane by pressing modifier+number: you might need other modifiers or conflicting modifiers. When “Emulate US Keyboard” is enabled, you can press the configured modifier plus the key on the top row that corresponds to a number key on a US keyboard. For example, on AZERTY, the & key would act as the 1 key." = "Some keyboard layouts (such as AZERTY) require a modifier to press a number key. This causes problems for switching to a window, tab, or split pane by pressing modifier+number: you might need other modifiers or conflicting modifiers. When “Emulate US Keyboard” is enabled, you can press the configured modifier plus the key on the top row that corresponds to a number key on a US keyboard. For example, on AZERTY, the & key would act as the 1 key.";

/* Keys: leader key help */
"The leader behaves like a modifier key, such as Command or Option, but is a separate keystroke. It can be used in key bindings. For example, if you set the leader to ⌘b then you could bind an action to the two-keystroke sequence “⌘b x”. ⌘b is the recommended leader and that keystroke will not be used for other purposes in the future." = "The leader behaves like a modifier key, such as Command or Option, but is a separate keystroke. It can be used in key bindings. For example, if you set the leader to ⌘b then you could bind an action to the two-keystroke sequence “⌘b x”. ⌘b is the recommended leader and that keystroke will not be used for other purposes in the future.";

